{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>an oven and ranges — it shall be broken down</b> - The verse comes to teach that the law of the oven and the ranges, which are made of clay and in which fire is kindled inside and bread is baked in them while they are attached to the ground, shall be like the law of earthen vessels, which are the pots and the jars baked in the kiln and are movable — that they too contract impurity and have no purification in a ritual bath. And it says \"it shall be broken down\" (יֻתָּץ) and did not say יִשָּׁבֵר, to teach that one need not break them down to the point where no clay is found in their breaking to scoop fire from a live coal, but rather one tears them down and does not rebuild them to perform their work. And to teach further that they contract impurity even though they are attached to the ground — and he shall tear down what he built. For the meaning of נְתִיצָה is the demolition of a structure, as in \"and you tore down the houses\" (Isaiah 22:10), \"and he shall tear down the house\" (Leviticus 14:45)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:01.268244602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}